      "name": "token-event-trace-then-delayed-plasticity",
      "runtime_change": "Stage 3A stores compact graph tokens and objective facts; Stage 3B-1 adds short-lived local activity eligibility; Stage 3B-2 records bootstrap delayed association candidates; Stage 3B-3 records rejectable parameter-family modulation proposals; Stage 3C-1 binds proposals to pre-activation local carriers; Stage 3C-2 emits bounded candidate deltas; Stage 3C-3 validates exact all-or-none shadow transactions; Stage 3C-4 permits explicitly opted-in short-window live writes with a bounded applied ledger and automatic rollback; Stage 3C-5 records score-free objective evidence for guarded-live and read-only control windows; Stage 3C-6 creates explicit shared-checkpoint branch identities and exports component-wise paired evidence outside the runtime; Stage 3C-7 assesses repeated paired exports for coverage, rollback/clipping integrity, count-cost matching and component-wise branch divergence without scalarization; Stage 3C-8 hierarchically aggregates windows within subjects and subjects within independent source checkpoints, then reports coordinate-wise sign, dispersion and interval stability without scalarization; Stage 3C-9 runs a short fixed-bootstrap paired data study with symmetric control admission and export-boundary transient finalization, without permanent retention; Stage 3C-10 adds external funnel, visibility, retention-coverage and branch-divergence diagnostics; Stage 3C-11 expands only independent source replication and audits sample adequacy without changing the mechanism or retention policy; Stage 3C-12 compares trace-safe branch horizons with exact prefix identity; Stage 3C-13 compares temporary exposure duration with identical source checkpoints and read-only control behavior; Stage 3C-14 compares one isolated fixed-bootstrap parameter-family target route with pre-bootstrap identity and no value or retention semantics; Stage 3C-15 externally diagnoses six-family local sensitivity, delayed-context dependence, clamp inactivity and eligibility reachability without runtime mutation; Stage 3C-16 isolates one existing edge-local eligibility carrier for the mechanically sensitive edge-forward family, preserving source/control identity, automatic rollback and score-free evidence without value or retention semantics. Stage 3C-20 isolates one fixed-bootstrap graph-state readout into association-visible token port 29, verifying source/control identity and temporal-versus-subject geometry without changing similarity, candidate allocation, update scale or retention. Stage 3C-21 isolates a readout-only objective-input coordinate that creates subject/event-specific association-visible geometry without action-output changes. Stage 3C-22 externally reconstructs the complete candidate opportunity and audits selected historical-event identity coverage and reuse concentration without runtime or checkpoint changes. Stage 3C-23 adds a common second readout-only node in an experiment-specific ten-node bootstrap and changes only its existing objective input between a duplicated rank-one control and a data-screened rank-two coordinate; action output, addressing, update, rollback and retention remain fixed. Stage 3C-24 externally reconstructs rank-one/rank-two candidate opportunity, score margins, selected historical-event identity coverage and reuse concentration without runtime or checkpoint changes. Stage 3C-25 externally separates absolute and normalized winner margins, candidate opportunity and deterministic winner-basin reuse in the frozen rank-two arm without runtime or checkpoint changes. Stage 3C-26 externally separates source-boundary forced assignments, historical age, query phase and opportunity-normalized winner occupancy in the same frozen rank-two arm without runtime or checkpoint changes. Stage 3C-27 externally separates source-boundary one-candidate forcing, exact latest-on-tie behavior and strict local visible-token geometry without runtime or checkpoint changes. Stage 3C-28 externally separates a shared discrete first-coordinate codebook, cross-subject transition synchrony, subject-anchored second-coordinate drift and within-subject recurrent winner basins without runtime or checkpoint changes. Stage 3C-29 externally conditions exact first-state transition-class replay and subject-anchored second-coordinate locality on multi-candidate opportunity, excluding source-boundary forced assignments and changing no runtime or checkpoint contract. Stage 3C-30 externally applies a predeclared zero/positive weight panel to the second visible coordinate over the identical authoritative candidate set, separating first-coordinate state occupancy from within-state identity ordering without runtime or checkpoint changes. Stage 3C-31 externally permutes the second visible coordinate across subjects while preserving its tick-wise marginal and authoritative candidate opportunity, separating coordinate distribution from subject-history binding without runtime mutation. Stage 3C-32 introduces an experiment-only runtime alignment policy with identical identity/cyclic-donor sort-copy paths and a four-arm shared-checkpoint guarded-live/read-only-control design; it verifies manipulation, matched candidate evaluation/storage, forced rollback and component-wise source-balanced difference-in-differences without retention or scalar value."
    },
